{
	"name": "Royal Jelly",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/slimes/slime-movement-pseudopods-green.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Royal jellies are believed to be a unique subspecies of gelatinous cube with an even more unique diet: They exclusively consume treasure, specifically precious metals like gold, silver, and platinum. They typically take on the color and metallic sheen of whatever their preferred metal is, and trinkets, coins, and other small items forged of that material can be found floating in their semi-transparent bodies.</p><p>The makeup of the royal jelly’s body creates a special environment that staves off rust and corrosion on the metals within them while also causing mild skin irritation when it comes into contact with most humanoids. Any adventurer attempting to snatch a trinket out of a royal jelly must succeed on a DC 14 Dexterity saving throw, taking 1d4 acid damage on a failure or half as much damage on a success. This particular property leads to royal jellies being a security staple of noble treasure rooms, bank vaults, and even dragon lairs.</p>",
